(1097864, 132015, 23458, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bear_music:</b></div><hr/><i> What is it? Sky, building, and a hue-shifted concrete wall, is what it looks like.<br/> <br/>Very nice.<br/> <br/>R. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You''ve got it in one. (I''m assuming your guess about my identity wasn''t as spot on :P)<br/> <br/>Just like to thank everyone who commented here - this is far and away my most sucessful shot here, and the feedback I''ve received has been really great. It''s nice to see the irony wasn''t lost on most :). <br/> <br/>Considering some of the incredibly great work by some really terrific photogs in this challenge, I couldn''t be happier with my placing. <br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Anders<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-01-09 04:57:37.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by bear_music: What is it? Sky, building, and a hue-shifted concrete wall, is what it looks like. Very nice. R.   You''ve got it in one. (I''m assuming your guess about my identity wasn''t as spot on :P) Just like to thank everyone who commented here - this is far and away my most sucessful shot here, and the feedback I''ve received has been really great. It''s nice to see the irony wasn''t lost on most :).  Considering some of the incredibly great work by some really terrific photogs in this challenge, I couldn''t be happier with my placing.  Cheers Anders', '2005-01-09 04:46:21.000000', '2005-01-09 04:57:37.000000', 0),
