(1102199, 132467, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by puma:</b></div><hr/><i> Either you are destroying money and should be arrested ... </i></td></tr></table> <br/>It is not illegal to destroy or even write on US currency, unless you attempt to defraud. If you have over half of the bill intact, you can obtain a replacement at a bank.<br/> <br/>If you light your cigar with a $100 bill, but only burn the end, it costs you nothing but some inconvenience.<br/> <br/>If you print out US currency as a prop, make it at least 25% larger or smaller than actual size, and only print one side on any sheet -- you should then be within the legal guidelines.<br/> <br/>Cool picture too!</td>', 'Originally posted by puma: Either you are destroying money and should be arrested ...  It is not illegal to destroy or even write on US currency, unless you attempt to defraud. If you have over half of the bill intact, you can obtain a replacement at a bank. If you light your cigar with a $100 bill, but only burn the end, it costs you nothing but some inconvenience. If you print out US currency as a prop, make it at least 25% larger or smaller than actual size, and only print one side on any sheet -- you should then be within the legal guidelines. Cool picture too!', '2005-01-11 19:46:34.000000', NULL, 0),
