(1120222, 132267, 19408, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by deapee:</b></div><hr/><i> OMG why did you put your credit card number on the internet!!!  That being said, i like the use of DOF.  The lighting seems a bit on the low side, but the composition and sharp focus makes up for it.  The credit card owner walking out the door is a nice addition to the scene -- as if he just cut up his card and is done with it.  Good work. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You''re right the lighting is too low. I didn''t notice it. After adjusting it looks better.</td>', 'Originally posted by deapee: OMG why did you put your credit card number on the internet!!!  That being said, i like the use of DOF.  The lighting seems a bit on the low side, but the composition and sharp focus makes up for it.  The credit card owner walking out the door is a nice addition to the scene -- as if he just cut up his card and is done with it.  Good work.   You''re right the lighting is too low. I didn''t notice it. After adjusting it looks better.', '2005-01-19 20:50:15.000000', NULL, 0),
